  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, describes The Telepathy Tapes, a 2024 project linked to people he names as Ky Dickens and Diane Powell, which tests whether autistic children who cannot speak can pick up their parents' thoughts. In his account, a parent looks at a random image made by an iPad, and the question is whether the child can tell what it is. If it works, minds could share information without any words at all."
